.LONG TERM...
Issued at 148 PM PST Tue Nov 17 2026
(Thursday through next Monday)

Rain showers and thunderstorm potential will diminish by Thursday
afternoon and evening. There may still be lingering showers over
the Pacific and adjacent inland areas through early Friday
morning. This will occur as the surface and mid/upper level low
push farther inland away from the Bay Area and Central Coast.
Temperatures are forecast to cool once again both Friday and
Saturday morning into the low-to-mid 30s in the North and East Bay
Valleys as well as the southern Salinas Valley.

Another cold front is forecast to approach the region on Saturday
as a low pressure system approaches the Pacific Northwest.
Rainfall from this system through Sunday is forecast to be
significantly less than this current system. Thus, the storm door
remains open! Remember to keep up-to-date with the latest forecast
information.

