.MARINE...
(Today through Sunday)
Issued at 148 PM PST Tue Nov 17 2026

Showers will linger over the coastal waters this morning with
brisk northwest winds. Meanwhile, a rapidly deepening low
pressure system will develop off the Pacific Northwest today and
tonight. A cold front with this low will arrive and slowly move
across the coastal waters and bays Wednesday with heavy rain and
wind. The low center will then follow through, it will bring more
rain Wednesday night and Thursday. Expect hazardous marine
conditions midweek with widespread gales, moderate to heavy rain
and a slight chance of thunderstorms. Localized storm force gusts
are possible Wednesday into Thursday. Another cold front with rain
and possibly gusty winds arrives Saturday and Saturday night.

